<h1>The Goal</h1>

<p>
    The goal of this project is to create continous and differentiable extentions of RuneScape's experiance functions
    that can be used to calculate decimal level values for any experiance value between \(0\) and \(200,000,000\).
</p>

<h1>The Details</h1>

<p>
    With the exception of the Invention skill, all skills use the following formula to determine how much xp is needed
    to reach a given level, \(L\).
</p>
<p>
    \[xp(L)=\left\lfloor\frac{1}{4}\sum_{n=1}^{L-1}\left\lfloor n+300*2^{\frac{n}{7}} \right\rfloor\right\rfloor\]
</p>
<p>
    For this project, this formula presents two problems. Firstly, summations are only defined for whole numbers.
    This could be rectified by 
    
    Firstly, \(\left\lfloor x\right\rfloor\) means the greatest integer
    less than or equal to \(x\), also known as the floor function.
</p>
<p>\[\begin{split}
    xp(L)&=\epsilon(L) + \frac{1}{4}\sum_{n=1}^{L-1}n+300*2^{\frac{n}{7}} \\
         &=\epsilon(L) + \frac{1}{4}\sum_{n=1}^{L-1}n+75\sum_{n=1}^{L-1}2^{\frac{n}{7}}\\
         &=\epsilon(L) + \frac{L(L-1)}{8}+75\frac{2^{\frac{L}{7}}-2^{\frac{1}{7}}}{2^{\frac{1}{7}}-1}
    \end{split}\]
</p>